    "summary": "Sansa made of split palm leaf rib joined at centre with resin ?. Set of nine cane tongues incised along lengths with geometric patterns. Tongues held in place by single cane stick bound with fibre strings which run through palm rib resonator; fibre string also knotted to ends of cane strip to form handle. Tongues supported at either end by triangular palm rib bridges. Surface of resonator incised with geometric patterns. Small triangular sound hole in centre of box.",
